      "problem": "Simplify $\\dfrac{1}{3}(3a+6b)+2a.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we apply the distributive law.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}(3a+6b)+2a & = \\\\ (\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot 3a+(\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot 6b+2a & = \\\\ \\frac{3a}{3}+\\frac{6b}{3}+2a & = \\\\ a+2b+2a & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we collect and combine the like terms, simplifying the coefficients as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+2b+2a & = \\\\ a+2a+2b & = \\\\ 3a+2b & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
